      "id": "10.3389/fmicb.2026.2007212",
      "title": "Genetic basis of Flavobacterium psychrophilum O-polysaccharide serotype specificity",
      "abstract": "The fish pathogen Flavobacterium psychrophilum exhibits extensive serological diversity associated with genetic variation in O-polysaccharide (O-PS) biosynthesis. To better define the repertoire of O-PS serotypes, the O-PS loci from 683 F. psychrophilum genome sequences were analyzed and compared to identify 29 genetic serotypes distributed among eight O-antigen polymerase (wzy) groups. Among these, 28 genetic serotypes spanning seven wzy groups shared the initiating glycosyltransferase gene responsible for the transfer of 2-acetamido-4-R-2,4-dideoxy-D-quinovose (D-Qui2NAc4NR) to a lipid carrier, together with one of six distinct gene sets for synthesis of the R-group in D-Qui2NAc4NR. In addition, 25 genetic serotypes across six wzy groups carried genes for the synthesis and transfer of 2-acetamido-2-deoxy-L-fucose (L-FucNAc) to D-Qui2NAc4NR. Among 17 genetic serotypes comprising wzy groups 1–3, 11 carried the glycosyltransferase gene responsible for the transfer of L-rhamnose (L-Rha) to L-FucNAc, thereby completing the trisaccharide repeat. The remaining six genetic serotypes in these groups carried an altered copy of this gene resulting from a 3.8-kb insertion that also introduced genes potentially involved in modification of the transferred L-Rha. Whereas wzy groups 1–3 shared the same flippase gene (wzx), each of four additional wzy groups, comprising 11 genetic serotypes, contained distinct flippase and glycosyltransferase genes. None of the serotype-variable genes from these seven wzy groups were present in the O-PS locus of the F. psychrophilum type strain, which constituted the eighth wzy group. Finally, all 29 genetic serotypes were accurately assigned in silico using a composite query sequence comprising concatenated 100-bp consensus fragments derived from serotype-variable genes. These findings establish a genetic framework for molecular serotyping and analysis of O-PS diversity in F. psychrophilum.",
