      "id": "10.3389/fmicb.2026.1996435",
      "title": "Antifungal activity and putative VOC-mediated inhibition of Botrytis fabiopsis by Streptomyces albidoflavus X13 isolated from Panax notoginseng",
      "abstract": "In a search for biocontrol agents against gray mold disease of Panax notoginseng, the Streptomyces albidoflavus strain X13 was isolated from healthy P. notoginseng leaves. In dual-culture assays, X13 inhibited the gray mold pathogen Botrytis fabiopsis by 65% and exhibited broad-spectrum antifungal activity against six other P. notoginseng pathogens; foliar application of X13 in pot experiments further achieved 99.52% control efficacy against gray mold. X13 possessed multiple plant growth-promoting traits, including ammonia production, growth on nitrogen-free medium, production of the phytohormones IAA and GA, and ACC deaminase activity, and secreted the extracellular enzymes protease, chitinase, and β-1,3-glucanase. Comparative assays showed that the antagonistic activity of X13 was mediated primarily by volatile organic compounds (VOCs) rather than non-volatile metabolites. Untargeted GC-MS metabolomics identified 154 differentially abundant VOCs, among which dimethyl trisulfide, 2-decanone, and nonanal emerged as the major candidate antifungal compounds, causing mycelial malformation of B. fabiopsis with EC50 values of 274.3, 1,087, and 1,120 μg/L, respectively (theoretical headspace estimates). These findings identify X13 as a promising microbial resource for the eco-friendly biocontrol of gray mold of P. notoginseng; the contribution of VOCs to its efficacy under in planta conditions remains to be verified.",
